quran[27]{c,v,t}:
  37,25,(It will be said to them:) ‘What is the matter with you that you do not help each other (now)?’
  37,26,"Rather, that Day, they will be entirely submissive!"
  37,27,"And some of them will turn to others, questioning each other."
  37,28,They (the misled followers) will say: ‘You came to us from a position of power (swearing an oath of being right).’
  37,29,They (the leaders) will answer: ‘No! You had disbelieved on your own.
  37,30,"We had no power over you. Instead, you yourselves were already a rebellious people."
  37,31,So the decree of our Lord against us is correct. We shall indeed taste (the punishment now).
  37,32,"So we caused you to deviate (from the right path), for we were deviant (ourselves).’"
  37,33,So on that Day they shall all share in the punishment.
  37,34,"Indeed, that is how We deal with the guilty."
  37,35,"Whenever it was said to them: ‘There is none worthy of worship except Allah,’ they used to show arrogance."
  37,36,And (they would) say: ‘Should we abandon our gods for a crazy poet?’
  37,37,"Instead, He has come with the truth and confirmed the (former) messengers."
  37,38,"Indeed, you shall taste the painful punishment."
  37,39,"And you will be rewarded only for what you used to do,"
  37,40,except the chosen (and purified) servants of Allah.
  37,41,"For them, there shall be known provision,"
  37,42,"fruits (of every kind), and they shall be highly honoured,"
  37,43,"in Gardens of Bliss,"
  37,44,"(seated) on couches, facing one another,"
  37,45,served with a cup (of sacred drink) passing around them from a pure flowing spring.
  37,46,(The drink will be) crystal white (and) delicious to the drinkers.
  37,47,Therein will be neither any headache nor will they be intoxicated.
  37,48,"And with them will be spouses of modest gazes, with beautiful lustrous eyes,"
  37,49,as if they were eggs (or pearls) carefully protected (from dust).
  37,50,"Then some of those (i.e. the residents of Paradise) will turn to one another, questioning each other."
  37,51,"One among them will say: ‘Indeed, I had a companion (in my worldly life),"
